# rpg/art/doll/maps/stamps/boots_youth.stamps: the youth's boot, ONE drawing in five tilts (docs/MOTION_P2.md 4.2, 5.5; STYLE_P2
# (KIN-YOUTH, P2b motion rollout 2026-10-22) Y1 gains a second toe-cap pixel (17 px: BOOTSIZE against Y2's 18 within 10 %),
# Y3 a flatter toe step (17 px, its thickness across the sole 2.7+: BOOTTILT), and Y9 is new: the run flight's trailing foot
# pointed (toe down and back along the shin, heel up at the ankle; Y0's 17 px turned ~125 deg by hand, 4 rows so the
# flight's sole clears 2 rows).

# 10 "The owner's motion reference"). The youth's own foot (kin/youth/legs/std's side idle: the B rows F-2..F-1, 5 and 6 px of

# leather over a 6 px Ink sole; the 4 px shaft above it is the shin, drawn by the leg), hand-placed at each tilt, never a

# shear, a squash or a tool rotation: Y0 flat (the planted foot); Y1 toe-up 1:2 (heel strike: the sole stepping 2 / 2 / 2 up

# to the toe, the toe cap a pixel above; 17 px); Y2 heel-up 1:2 (motion fix round 2, R2-06: the walk contact's trailing foot

# up on its toe pad, the heel TWO rows up so it reads at 1x: the sole stepping 2 / 2 / 2, 18 px); Y3 toe-off (rolled onto

# the toe, the sole stepping 1 / 2 / 2: the down frame's trailing foot, the run's kick, push and flight; 17 px); Y4 pointed

# (fix round 2: Y2 rolled onto its toe tip, the sole 2 / 2 / 1 and the tip's outline below the last step: the walk pass's

# swing foot, toe down a row off the ground, its single toe pixel clear of the planted toe; 18 px). Every key keeps the

# square heel, the outline all round, the straight Ink sole, the lit pixel behind the heel outline. `n` near, `f` far (a

# value darker, the same silhouette). origin = the key's ground pivot on its sole row (the heel of Y0 / Y1, the toe's last

# Ink pixel of Y2 / Y3 / Y4). L entries: the R keys mirrored and re-lit for the top-left light (never the plain mirror).

# Used by kin/youth/legs/std.pxm and tips.pxm (`# put` comments, expanded there pixel for pixel).
use person

# Y0 flat (the planted foot; the run's landing and the flight's leading foot, lifted), R view: origin = the heel

stamp Y0n R origin 0 2
|fihgf.
|fihhgf
|KKKKKK
regions
|BBBBB.
|BBBBBB
|OOOOOO

stamp Y0f R origin 0 2
|fhggf.
|fhhggf
|KKKKKK
regions
|BBBBB.
|BBBBBB
|OOOOOO

